Overall, the selected DEB-TKTD model reproduced the concentration-dependent responses observed for juvenile growth, adult growth, and reproduction (Figure 10.21 & Figure 10.19). The model captured the general magnitude and shape of the decline in life-history performance with increasing epoxiconazole exposure. However, some systematic deviations remained. Growth effects were underestimated at the lowest tested concentrations, between 0.928 and 9.28 mg\(\cdot\)kg\(^{-1}\), resulting in predicted growth values above the observations. Reproductive effects were also underestimated at the highest concentrations, between 43.1 and 200 mg\(\cdot\)kg\(^{-1}\), with predicted cocoon production exceeding the observed values. Despite these discrepancies, the combined assimilation and reproduction pMoA provided an overall satisfactory description of epoxiconazole effects across the three endpoints.

